<tbody>
<tr>
<td>
<p>Establish the college as a national model for AI, cybersecurity and computing education through future-ready curricula that adapt quickly to technological change and ensure every graduate is career-ready.&nbsp;</p>
</td>
<td>
<table class="media-large">
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable">News - Image - Large <br />One Column, Image Width: 1000px, Height: 405 px* <br />Two Column, Image Width: 735px, Height: 405 px* <br />* Recommended Height.</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td class="image"><img src="/images/news/placeholder/news-large-image.jpg" alt="" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h4>Strategies</h4>
<table class="two-column-text">
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable" width="50%">Column 1</th>
<th class="ou-help mceNonEditable" width="50%">Column 2</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>
<ul>
<li>Academic programs and upskilling &ndash; Grow and ensure AI-integration in core majors (cyberecurity, AI, computer science, information technology, computer science and engineering); curricula grounded in computer science and cybersecurity engineering fundamentals as AI is built upon the enduring discipline of computer science; integrate ethics-by-design; launch computer science and engineering major, and interdisciplinary computing degrees; seek accreditation, expand concentrations, minors and stackable certificates; offer no‑code/low‑code/high‑code upskilling for non-computer science learners.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Enable student progression: Build semester schedules that are tied to student graduation plans, reduce class section sizes, provide targeted success coaching for retention, expand AI-based learning opportunities, and efficiently use TA support.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Tech Career Advancement Program (tCAP): Implement and operationalize the career advancement program. tCAP will integrate advising, experiential learning and employer partnerships into every stage of a student&rsquo;s academic journey, ensuring students graduate with strong technical foundations and applied skills, professional networks and the confidence to succeed in a rapidly evolving tech landscape.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
</td>
<td>
<ul>
<li>Faculty development: Support faculty with training in emerging technologies and teaching innovation to ensure instructional excellence.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Predictive advising: Move from &ldquo;clinic&rdquo; based advising to a more proactive/predictive advising model; each student has a designated primary advisor; graduation plans for all at all time; monitor mid-term grades in all undergraduate courses, identify at-risk students, provide outreach to them, and refer them to tutoring support; identify, reach out to, support, and monitor graduates for the following two semesters; implement rule where student non-response or inaction results in a registration hold, starting as early as at the end of the first year.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h4><span style="color: #3f565e; font-size: 1.125em;">Success Indicators:&nbsp;</span></h4>
<ul>
<li>Retention: Maintain first-year retention rate of &gt; 94% and academic progress rate (2nd-year retention with GPA &ge; 2.0) of at least 92%.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Four-year graduation rate (FTIC): Maintain or exceed the USF institutional goal of 70%, ensuring the college contributes to the system-wide goal of 70%&nbsp;</li>
<li>Experiential learning: Achieve 100% undergraduate participation in experiential learning.&nbsp;</li>
<li>Degrees awarded in strategic emphasis: Track the number of degrees awarded in STEM fields (CIP 11), ensuring 100% alignment with the Board of Governors' Programs of Strategic Emphasis.</li>
</ul><!-- /com.omniupdate.div --></maincontent>

